{
  "description": "Installation of a French drain adjacent to the external front wall at basement level within the front courtyard of 93 Balls Pond Road, a grade 2 listed terraced house within the De Beauvoir Conservation Area. \n\nThe works are intended to address damp affecting the front wall by improving drainage and reducing water collecting against the historic masonry. The existing concrete courtyard surface appears to have been raised above its original level and is considered to contribute to moisture penetration. \n\nThe proposal is to remove concrete immediately adjacent the wall, expose the ground beneath and excavate a trench c.300m deep. A perforated drainage pipe would be laid within the trench ad directed into nearby drains. The trench would be backfilled with pea shingle to ground level and left uncovered. \n\nThe works would be undertaken carefully to protect the historic wall and foundations. Any disturbed wall finishes would be repaired using materials compatible with the existing lime render and breathable finish. \n\nThe works are confined to the front courtyard. No works are proposed to the rear elevations, and there would be no change to residential use or existing access arrangements. ",
